  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Pipenzolate is a synthetic anticholinergic (quaternary ammonium) antispasmodic drug intended for functional gastrointestinal disorders, and has also been combined with psycholeptics for such conditions. It is not an approved medicine; it is considered investigational and does not appear to be marketed in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2096435&quot;>Wikidata Q2096435</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>pipenzolate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A03AB14</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13844&quot;>DB13844</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/4832&quot;>4832</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:95178&quot;>95178</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2096435&quot;>Q2096435</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C22H28NO3+</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>354.47 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
